Known product bugs behind refusals this run (not new findings - do not baseline):
  token_denom deadlock on concurrent splits (Go map order): 33 refusal(s) in FT-01 (11), QCAP-01 (13), WALLET-PREP (9)
    two splits or pledges at once on one DID - a quorum pledging fractional amounts for several transfers, or one wallet deploying or minting several things - update its token_denom rows one by one in Go map order, which is random (core/wallet/persist_genesis_tx.go:209, post_consensus_persistence.go:716), so Postgres finds a lock cycle and kills one. Sorting the denominations before the updates removes it. A pledge also decrements token_denom in a second DB transaction after the pledge itself is committed (core/pledge_v2.go:287): when that one fails, the counter stays above the real Free tokens
  zero clock tolerance (checks.go:61): 1 refusal(s) in CHAIN-01 (1)
    the quorum rejects a transaction stamped even a second ahead of its own clock (core/consensus/checks.go:61, Epoch > time.Now()), so any clock difference between sender and quorum refuses transfers


